                            <comment id="17218958" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 22 Oct 2020 11:45:35 +0000"  >&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Tests fail only on some recent JDK versions where cgroup limits are supported&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Both .NET and Java have the logic &quot;Data Region Max Size = 20% of available RAM&quot;, Java side uses &lt;tt&gt;OperatingSystemMXBean.totalPhysicalMemorySize&lt;/tt&gt;, .NET does not have a native way, so we read from /proc/meminfo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
